<p>Hi, author.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I have some major issues with this. Mainly, you seem intent on &quot;porting&quot; a skip concept to a tale without really providing a fresh perspective or appeal that can't be found in the original. I think you want the time travel angle to offer new ideas, but I don't see that working very well. Why would time travel be more interesting than watching the story through a play? In fact, this seems to undercut the original significantly, since part of the appeal of HKT is that it's a fictional play, and thus its effects are more mysterious. Setting the same plot in the real world past doesn't add anything, and indeed seems to make the idea more shallow.</p>
<p>I think it is possible to explore this skip's narrative in Tale form, but I do believe you would need to bring something more unique to the table for that to be viable.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Have a good day!</p>

