			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857867">
									

<p>Offering my two cents as the author, I believe you unfortunately misread the whole article.</p>
<p>So, the first point. It's not anomalous, you say. For context, this article takes place in 2022, two years after the bushfires have occurred. Safe to say, if thousands of koalas<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-787646-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-787646-1')">1</a></sup> still disappear at that point, without any fires, that would be utterly anomalous, right? I mean, it's the symbol of Australia, and someone's bound to notice the fact that they're disappearing.</p>
<p>Plus, I don't think large, flying serpents are a species native to Australia, because if that's the case, then I would be saving up in order to ride on those. Second, koalas are cute, and I won't trade those for snakes.</p>
<p>Second, I'm not sure on your thoughts about the pacing. You say &quot;greatly written&quot; at the start but then dismiss my article's pacing and narrative as a joke.</p>
<p>Choose one - it's ok if you found the article unsatisfying, but I'm just really confused about what you said.</p>
<p>Additionally, all people I asked did not point out that my article was too sparse and unnaturally progressing, and I'm against the idea that environmental action against climate change is a joke, so I have my doubts on everything you said.</p>
<p>Lastly, the ending (Incident DROPBEAR) was crafted in order to suit the New Year. Look, I don't want to shoehorn drama, politics<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-787646-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-787646-2')">2</a></sup> and angst into this whole thing just to reduce the possible &quot;that's it?&quot;moment, because that would detract from the whole koala and aboriginal culture angle.</p>
<p>Plus, I'm simply basing off the fact that Dreamtime is rooted in the concept of an everywhen - the fact that it is timeless, so I actually don't feel good about you saying that this is a joke.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-787646-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-787646-1')">1</a>. You should also note that even those in zoos - safe from bushfires - disappeared.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-787646-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-787646-2')">2</a>. Australian politics are a whole another level, and as a Filipino, I didn't dare touch on that deeply.</div>
</div>

