														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857823">
									

<p>Thanks for your response I do really appreciate the feedback. I'll try and answer your questions as much as I can.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Response</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First the blood is the base anomaly. The first type discovered. I didn't mention this part in the initial post (which may be why it's more confusing) but the non-linear time of the dimension effects the blood, meaning it cannot age. As well as the ability to suck humes out of an enviroment.</p>
<p>The second blood isn't really another type of the scp, it's more like state of it 'awakened'. the higher the hume level the dimension has the less nonlinear time is. This effects the blood's own ageless property, causing it to change and go 'bad'.</p>
<p>The overuse of classification is a mistake, especially the dimension and the additional instance within the dimension is unnecessary and I'm gonna rethink that part. Also the hard science SRA babble isn't the clearest way to get across what the SCP does.</p>
<p>As for the containment procedures housing the 'awakened' blood would have to be using SRAs in a distanced wing of a site. Any blood that becomes awakened in the field needs to be recovered asap.</p>
<p>Additionally the main theme I wish to hit is there in the title. Cognation, from <strong>cognate</strong> which can be defined in a number of ways:</p>
<ol>
<li>Related by blood; having a common ancestor.</li>
<li>Related in origin, as certain words in genetically related languages descended from the same ancestral root; for example, English <em>red</em> and Sanskrit <em>rudhirá</em> meaning red, bloody.</li>
<li>Related or analogous in nature, character, or function.</li>
</ol>
<p>The critical theme is the relation by blood, in both a literal and metanarrative sense. Blood connecting the girls from 231, Anna Lang and Robert Scranton.</p>
<p>The article itself would act as a relation by blood. Of Robert Scranton and The Scarlet King.</p>
<p>As for the significance for the wider universe, the Foundation could have been feeding/creating one of it's most infamous antagonists, unknowingly or knowingly. By using one of their own doctors no less.</p>
<p>Kind of going for the idea the foundation is forced into a hard situation. As a result a mixture of desperation and necessity causes them to use the blood large scale to contain reality benders.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope this is helpful and that it explains a lot more.</p>

							</div>

								
					
