<p><em>This</em> is a beautiful dog story. It's hard to go wrong with dog stories. Their simple minds and big hearts make them endearing protagonists immediately. I've already read the skip this is based on, and a graphic novel centered around Laika, so I'm already very invested in this adorable, tragic little dog. This delivers on that investment. A dog contemplating its own death is… not fun. And very well executed. Bravo.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Nothing to add. Bravo x2, and a +1 as well.</p>

